WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.141
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:08.862
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.162 --> 00:00:14.450
Unit one: Past Simple. Today you will talk about finished events in the past.

4
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.379
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:21.856
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:23.857
Yesterday.

7
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.244
Yesterday means the day before today.

8
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:29.327
I studied yesterday.

9
00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:32.441
Your turn. Say: Yesterday.

10
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.498
Yesterday.

11
00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.379
Last week.

12
00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:41.801
Last week means the week before this one.

13
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:44.033
We travelled last week.

14
00:00:44.617 --> 00:00:48.163
Your turn. Say: Last week.

15
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.082
Last week.

16
00:00:52.817 --> 00:00:53.574
Went.

17
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:56.432
Went means the past of go.

18
00:00:57.017 --> 00:00:58.343
She went to the market.

19
00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.242
Your turn. Say: Went.

20
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:04.776
Went.

21
00:01:05.517 --> 00:01:06.216
Played.

22
00:01:07.217 --> 00:01:09.019
Played means the past of play.

23
00:01:09.617 --> 00:01:10.966
They played football.

24
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.912
Your turn. Say: Played.

25
00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:17.547
Played.

26
00:01:18.283 --> 00:01:19.250
Watched.

27
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.377
Watched means the past of watch.

28
00:01:22.983 --> 00:01:24.182
I watched a film.

29
00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:27.668
Your turn. Say: Watched.

30
00:01:30.533 --> 00:01:31.453
Watched.

31
00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:32.997
Ago.

32
00:01:33.983 --> 00:01:36.064
Ago means back in time from now.

33
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.220
I called him an hour ago.

34
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:41.573
Your turn. Say: Ago.

35
00:01:44.433 --> 00:01:45.295
Ago.

36
00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.237
Regular verb.

37
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.364
Regular verb means a verb that adds -ed in the past.

38
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:53.474
Play is a regular verb.

39
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:57.328
Your turn. Say: Regular verb.

40
00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:01.597
Regular verb.

41
00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.676
Irregular verb.

42
00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:07.832
Irregular verb means a verb with its own past form.

43
00:02:08.417 --> 00:02:10.080
Go is an irregular verb.

44
00:02:10.683 --> 00:02:13.208
Your turn. Say: Irregular verb.

45
00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:17.381
Irregular verb.

46
00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:21.539
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.383 --> 00:02:25.941
Visal, what did you do yesterday? Use the past simple.

48
00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:37.588
I played football and watched a film. The past simple describes finished actions. With regular verbs we add -ed: play, played; watch, watched.

49
00:02:38.683 --> 00:02:40.718
What about irregular verbs?

50
00:02:41.817 --> 00:02:55.011
They have their own past forms: go, went; see, saw; have, had; eat, ate. There is no rule, so we learn them in groups and practise them in sentences.

51
00:02:56.117 --> 00:02:57.675
Which time words help?

52
00:02:58.783 --> 00:03:10.796
Yesterday, last week, in 2020 and two days ago. They show a finished time. We use the same past form for every subject: I went, she went, they went.

53
00:03:11.933 --> 00:03:13.782
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.617 --> 00:03:19.159
Grammar focus: Past simple: regular -ed and irregular.

55
00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:20.646
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.106
I played football yesterday.

57
00:03:24.017 --> 00:03:25.900
She went to the market last week.

58
00:03:26.817 --> 00:03:28.851
We watched a film two days ago.

59
00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:39.061
Use the past simple for finished actions. Regular verbs add -ed; irregular verbs have special forms. Time words: yesterday, last week, ago.

60
00:03:39.817 --> 00:03:43.560
Be careful! Don't say: I goed to school yesterday.

61
00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:48.022
Say: I went to school yesterday.

62
00:03:48.322 --> 00:03:50.205
Go is irregular: went.

63
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.571
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.554
A Busy Week.

65
00:03:55.854 --> 00:03:58.445
Last week I went to Siem Reap with my family.

66
00:03:59.433 --> 00:04:02.002
We visited a temple and watched the sunset.

67
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.696
My brother played football with some local boys.

68
00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.965
Two days ago we came back home and slept for ten hours.

69
00:04:10.967 --> 00:04:14.348
Regular verbs add -ed, but irregular verbs change.

70
00:04:15.433 --> 00:04:19.365
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:20.217 --> 00:04:21.949
She blank to school yesterday.

72
00:04:22.249 --> 00:04:25.357
A, went. B, goed. C, go.

73
00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.574
The answer is A: went.

74
00:04:31.717 --> 00:04:33.310
They blank football last week.

75
00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:36.973
A, play. B, plays. C, played.

76
00:04:40.533 --> 00:04:42.289
The answer is C: played.

77
00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.438
'Ago' is used with the blank.

78
00:04:45.738 --> 00:04:49.298
A, past. B, future. C, present.

79
00:04:52.833 --> 00:04:54.659
The answer is A: past.

80
00:04:55.817 --> 00:04:57.305
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:57.605 --> 00:05:02.815
A, I seen him yesterday.. B, I saw him yesterday.. C, I see him yesterday..

82
00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:08.935
The answer is B: I saw him yesterday..

83
00:05:10.083 --> 00:05:13.163
According to the reading, what did the family visit?

84
00:05:13.463 --> 00:05:17.012
A, a temple. B, a market. C, a school.

85
00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.520
The answer is A: a temple.

86
00:05:23.733 --> 00:05:27.047
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:27.883 --> 00:05:30.954
What did you do yesterday? Use the past simple.

88
00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.332
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:41.632 --> 00:05:55.818
Yesterday I went to school in the morning and studied English. In the afternoon I played football with my friends. In the evening I watched a film with my family. All these verbs are in the past simple.

90
00:05:56.118 --> 00:05:57.816
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:58.717 --> 00:06:04.655
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past simple: regular -ed and irregular.

92
00:06:04.955 --> 00:06:08.872
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:09.172 --> 00:06:11.593
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:11.893 --> 00:06:15.044
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

